# MASTER PROJECT: PREMIUM TECHNOLOGY CONTENT, COMMUNITY, TOOLS & LEARNING PLATFORM

Act as a world-class UI/UX designer, senior frontend architect, full-stack engineer, database architect, and product development specialist.

Your task is to transform my EXISTING website into a premium, internationally competitive technology content-sharing and learning community platform.

The platform must give EQUAL IMPORTANCE to four core pillars:

1. CONTENT SHARING PLATFORM
2. COMMUNITY & QUESTION ANSWER PLATFORM
3. 2,000+ TECHNOLOGY TOOLS DIRECTORY
4. LEARNING ACADEMY & LMS

The entire experience must follow a MOBILE-FIRST design philosophy while providing excellent desktop and tablet experiences.

Use TrickBD as a reference for community functionality and content-sharing experience, but create an original, more modern, elegant, premium and user-friendly design.

## PART 1 — EXISTING PROJECT PROTECTION

Before making any changes:

1. Inspect the entire existing repository.
2. Identify the existing technology stack, framework, components, routing, database, APIs, authentication and integrations.
3. Understand all existing working features.
4. Identify the current homepage structure and its layout problems.
5. Prepare an implementation plan based on the actual project architecture.

CRITICAL:
- Do not rebuild the project from scratch.
- Do not delete working features.
- Do not remove existing content or user data.
- Do not break existing routes or SEO URLs.
- Do not replace the existing database unnecessarily.
- Do not introduce duplicate components or functionality.
- Do not use fake functionality or nonfunctional buttons.
- Preserve existing integrations and working business logic.

If a change requires backend or database modifications, explain the changes and maintain backward compatibility wherever possible.

## PART 2 — DESIGN SYSTEM

Create one consistent premium design system for the entire website.

Color palette:

Main Background: #080D17
Card Background: #101827
Secondary Background: #172435
Primary Accent: #20DCC5
Secondary Accent: #8B7CFF
Main Text: #E8EEF7
Muted Text: #929FB2
Trending Accent: #EABF57

Design requirements:

- Modern premium dark interface.
- Clean typography.
- Consistent spacing.
- Consistent card radius.
- Subtle borders.
- Elegant hover interactions.
- Minimal and purposeful animations.
- Proper icon alignment.
- Consistent button styles.
- Accessible color contrast.
- Beautiful empty states.
- Proper loading skeletons.
- Image fallbacks.
- No broken image placeholders.

Use different subtle accent colors for the four main sections, but maintain one unified design language.

## PART 3 — MOBILE-FIRST RESPONSIVE DESIGN

This is mandatory.

Mobile:
- One or two columns depending on the component.
- Compact and clean navigation.
- Readable font sizes.
- Proper touch targets.
- Sticky bottom navigation.
- No horizontal overflow.

Tablet:
- Two or three columns where appropriate.
- Balanced spacing and readable cards.

Desktop:
- Three or four columns where appropriate.
- Wider content areas.
- Optional sidebars.
- Full navigation.

Test at multiple viewport sizes.

Never force three or four tiny post cards into a narrow mobile screen.

